 "notes": "Headline measured limit is the PILOT curve (blue) in Fig.9 (SpotLimit_5-14-21.pdf) and Fig.12: 5 sigma exclusion on the dark-photon kinetic mixing epsilon=chi from ~3.8 hours of real-time data over 50-300 MHz, using the room-temperature proof-of-concept setup. Curve extracted by vectorizing the blue polyline (2591 segments) and calibrating against axis tick labels; converted frequency->mass via m=h*f (50 MHz->2.07e-7 eV, 300 MHz->1.24e-6 eV) and log10(epsilon)->epsilon. 90 points, per-bin median of the jagged curve; median epsilon ~1.5e-12 consistent with abstract (epsilon~1e-12). Paper reports epsilon (kinetic mixing chi) directly, dimensionless, reported as-is (not chi^2). Density-dependent (eps ~ 1/sqrt(rho_DM)); paper assumes rho_DM=380+/-180 TeV/m^3 = 0.38 GeV/cm^3, not rescaled. Paper states 5 sigma; confidence_level field set to 0.95 (nearest allowed value). The Phase-I (green), Phase-II (black dashed), and orange spot-check dots (extrapolated to 1 month) are projections and are NOT reported.",
